<p>Work began on September 1, 1881. The east approach span was finished on May 9, 1882; the west approach on June 3; and the center span on October 18. The bridge cost $1.08 million. Between 200 and 600 men worked on the project at any given time, depending on the stage of construction.</p>

<p>The original spans had flat tops. They were replaced in 1905 after improved locomotives began carrying loads that exceeded the first design's capacity. Sturdier, arched trusses were erected on the existing piers and remain in service.</p>

